# The element is stored, then the barrier tests the state byte of the array. The call behind the rare edge gets the array and the element that was stored.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="put" role=Source
# CHECK-NOT: collectorState
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[storage]] = Load(b@[[list]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:JSObject_butterfly, {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK-NOT: collectorState
# CHECK: Store(b@[[entry]], b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:indexedContiguousProperties, {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[threshold]] = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = {{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:collectorState, {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[state]] = Load8Z(b@[[list]], offset = 7, ControlDependent|Reads:collectorState, {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[isUnmarked]] = Below(b@[[threshold]], b@[[state]], {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isUnmarked]], Terminal, {{*}}:PutArrayElement)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#[[done]], Else:Rare:#[[remember]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[done]]:
# CHECK: Return(Terminal)
# CHECK: BB#[[remember]]:
# CHECK: Patchpoint(b@[[list]]:Register({{*}}), b@[[entry]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = WarmAny, ControlDependent|Writes:{collectorState,
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The test of the storage kind, the bounds check, the store and the barrier. The count includes the six instructions of the unlikely arm that appends at the end of the array.
# X64: instructions: 14, patchpoints: 0
# ARM64: instructions: 16, patchpoints: 0
